      refused: spec-baseline allows 16 KB of threadgroup memory per block; the identity floor (profile 1) needs 32 KB, because the block size it buys decides the replication factor and the replication factor decides which partial sums combine

  identity floor, profile 1 :  32 KB threadgroup, 32 logical lanes, block 512 , threadgroup int atomics.
  FROZEN. A vendor that misses it is refused for IDENTICAL and runs FAST; the floor never drops to fit one, because dropping it changes every model already produced under this profile.
